gy Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around mid-2024.\n\n## Cloud Logging and Index Template Updates\n\nThe Cloud Logging component at SAP has been updated to improve index template and index pattern for metric-otel-v1-* indices. This proactive approach helps safeguard SAP against potential operational pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective logging not only prevents operational anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (244), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 29), (2024, 02, 29))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition, has been updated with several new features, including enhanced email notification domains, new wizard layouts in workspaces, public workspace access levels for non-members, and search results for non-members. These updates aim to improve user experience and operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (3611, 3612, 3613, 3614, 3615, 3616, 3617, 3618), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 11), (2024, 01, 25))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning Updates\n\nThe Identity Provisioning component at SAP has been updated with several new features, including query parameter membersType in Proxy System SCIM API, renamed system, and warning message in target systems. These updates aim to improve operational efficiency and user experience. [Data: Sources (3367, 3368, 3369), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 20), (2024, 02, 28))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nThe Cloud Identity Services component at SAP has been updated with several new features, including OpenID Connect, regular upgrade, and subject name identifier. These updates aim to improve operational efficiency and user experience. [Data: Sources (3364, 3365, 3366), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 28), (2024, 02, 28))]\n\n## SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration Updates\n\nThe SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration component at SAP has been updated with a new API available on SAP Business Accelerator Hub. This update aims to improve operational efficiency and user experience. [Data: Sources (3370), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 28), (2024, 02, 28))]", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's cloud services, highlighting key components, their environments, and recent updates. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud operations as of 2024.\n\n## Cloud Logging and Monitoring\n\nSAP Cloud Logging provides real-time monitoring and logging capabilities for cloud-based applications. Recent updates include improved index templates and index patterns for metric-otel-v1-* indices [Data: Sources (244), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 29), (2024, 02, 29))]. This enhancement enables more efficient log analysis and troubleshooting, supporting SAP's cloud operations and customer support services.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Updates\n\nSAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition, has received updates to improve user experience and functionality. The Application Group widget now behaves consistently across different access points [Data: Sources (245), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 29))]. Additionally, company administrators can define role-based access to workspaces for non-members [Data: Sources (246), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 22), (2024, 02, 29))]. These updates enhance the overall user experience and improve collaboration within the platform.\n\n## Cloud Identity Services Updates\n\nCloud Identity Services has undergone several updates, including the introduction of OpenID Connect [Data: Sources (247), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 28), (2024, 02, 28))]. This feature enables public clients for resource owner password credentials flow, JWT bearer flow, and token exchange flow. Additionally, Identity Authentication has been upgraded [Data: Sources (248), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 28), (2024, 02, 28))]. These updates improve the overall security and functionality of Cloud Identity Services.\n\n## Identity Provisioning Updates\n\nIdentity Provisioning has received updates, including the introduction of the convertTimezoneCode function [Data: Sources (249), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 08, 27))]. This function enables the conversion of timezone attributes into another format. Additionally, the Microsoft Azure Active Directory connector has been renamed to Microsoft Entra ID [Data: Sources (250), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 08, 27))]. These updates improve the overall functionality and user experience of Identity Provisioning.\n\n## Pricing Service Updates\n\nPricing Service has received updates, including the correction of an issue where the pricing service used not to re-evaluate the requirement formula based on updated attributes [Data: Sources (251), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 08, 27))]. This update ensures accurate pricing outcomes. Additionally, the document pricing requirement formula reevaluation has been improved [Data: Sources (252), Date_Range ((2025, 08, 27), (2025, 08, 27))]. These updates improve the overall functionality and accuracy of Pricing Service.\n\n## SAP Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has received updates, including the improvement of the machine learning model for payment advice documents [Data: Sources (253), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 04), (2025, 09, 04))]. This update enhances the overall accuracy and efficiency of SAP Document AI. Additionally, several code and stability improvements have been made [Data: Sources (254), Date_Range ((2025, 09, 04), (2025, 09, 04))]. These updates improve the overall functionality and user experience of SAP Document AI.", "# SAP Cloud Services Overview as of 2024-02-29\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP Cloud Services, highlighting key components, their relationships, and significant updates as of 2024-02-29. The information is relevant to SAP's cloud-based offerings and their evolution.\n\n## Cloud Logging and Monitoring\n\nCloud Logging and Monitoring are essential components of SAP Cloud Services, enabling users to track and analyze system performance, identify issues, and optimize resource utilization. The service provides real-time logging, monitoring, and alerting capabilities, ensuring that system administrators can respond promptly to any issues that may arise. Effective logging and monitoring are crucial for maintaining system reliability, security, and performance. [Data: Sources (244), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 29), (2024, 02, 29))]\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone and Advanced Edition\n\nSAP Build Work Zone and Advanced Edition are key components of SAP Cloud Services, providing a collaborative platform for users to create, manage, and share content. The service offers a range of features, including workspace management, content creation, and collaboration tools. The Advanced Edition provides additional features, such as role-based access control, custom domains, and support for external users. [Data: Sources (3111, 3112, 3113, 3114, 3115, 3116, 3117), Date_Range ((2024, 04, 18), (2024, 04, 18))]\n\n## Cloud Identity Services\n\nCloud Identity Services is a critical component of SAP Cloud Services, providing identity and access management capabilities for users and applications. The service offers a range of features, including user authentication, authorization, and provisioning. Cloud Identity Services ensures that users have secure and controlled access to SAP Cloud Services, protecting sensitive data and preventing unauthorized access. [Data: Sources (3364, 3365, 3366, 3367, 3368, 3369), Date_Range ((2024, 02, 28), (2024, 02, 28))]\n\n## SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration\n\nSAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration is a key component of SAP Cloud Services, providing credit risk management capabilities for users. The service offers a range of features, including credit scoring, credit reporting, and credit monitoring. SAP S/⁠4HANA Cloud for Credit Integration enables users to make informed credit decisions, reducing the risk of bad debt and improving cash flow. [Data: Sources (2865, 2866), Date_Range ((2024, 05, 23), (2024, 05, 23))]\n\n## Kyma Runtime\n\nKyma Runtime is a critical component of SAP Cloud Services, providing a platform for building, deploying, and managing cloud-native applications. The service offers a range of features, including containerization, orchestration, and service mesh capabilities. Kyma Runtime enables users to build and deploy scalable, secure, and high-performance applications, improving business agility and competitiveness. [Data: Sources (891), Date_Range ((2025, 04, 30), (2025, 05, 14))]\n\n## API Management\n\nAPI Management is a key component of SAP Cloud Services, providing a platform for designing, deploying, and managing APIs. The service offers a range of features, including API security, analytics, and monetization capabilities. API Management enables users to create and manage APIs that are secure, scalable, and high-performance, improving business agility and competitiveness. [Data: Sources (897), Date_Range ((2025, 05, 11), (2025, 05, 11))]", "# SAP Technology Overview as of 2024-10-31\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP's key technology components, highlighting their relationships and core attributes. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations as of 2024-10-31.\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone Capabilities\n\nSAP Build Work Zone, an advanced edition, is a key component of SAP's technology stack. It offers various features, including App Finder Enhancements, Content Export Enhancements, and Enhanced Page Builder. These capabilities support the creation and management of workspaces, content export, and page design, respectively. The latest revision of SAP Build Work Zone, as of 2024-10-31, is Version 2410B [Data: Sources (2014, 2015, 2017), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31))].\n\n## SAP Alert Notification Service Integrations\n\nThe SAP Alert Notification Service has been integrated with OpenSearch Enhanced with OpenSearch Dashboards and SAP Cloud Logging service. These integrations enable the service to provide enhanced notification capabilities and logging support. The latest revision of the SAP Alert Notification Service, as of 2024-10-31, is Version Cloud [Data: Sources (2011, 2012), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31))].\n\n## Cloud Foundry Updates\n\nCloud Foundry, a key environment for SAP's technology components, has been updated from 43.6.0 to 44.0.0. This update provides enhanced features and support for SAP's technology stack. The latest revision of Cloud Foundry, as of 2024-10-21, is Version 44.0.0 [Data: Source (2013), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 21))].", "# SAP Technology Updates Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report delves into SAP's key technology updates, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to enhance operational efficiency and user experience. The information is relevant to SAP's technology operations around 2024.\n\n## SAP Alert Notification Service Updates\n\nThe SAP Alert Notification Service has been updated to integrate with OpenSearch Enhanced with OpenSearch Dashboards [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))]. This integration enables users to find information about the integration of SAP Alert Notification service with OpenSearch. The update also includes a new version of the service, Cloud, which provides enhanced features and capabilities. [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))].\n\n## SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime Updates\n\nThe SAP BTP, Cloud Foundry Runtime has been updated to version 44.0.0 [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 21), (2024, 10, 31))]. This update includes several enhancements, such as improved performance and security features. The update also includes a new version of the service, Cloud, which provides enhanced features and capabilities. [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 21), (2024, 10, 31))].\n\n## SAP Build Work Zone, Advanced Edition Updates\n\nThe SAP Build Work Zone, Advanced Edition has been updated to include several new features and enhancements [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))]. These updates include improved user experience, enhanced collaboration tools, and improved security features. The update also includes a new version of the service, 2410B, which provides enhanced features and capabilities. [Data: Sources (417, 418), Date_Range ((2024, 10, 31), (2024, 10, 31))].\n\n## Deprecation of Container-Based Applications Pipeline\n\nThe Container-Based Applications pipeline has been deprecated and will be removed from the service on December 31st, 2024 [Data: Sources (1686), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 31), (2024, 12, 31))]. Existing jobs will continue to function until this date. We recommend using the Kyma Runtime pipeline instead. [Data: Sources (1686), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 31), (2024, 12, 31))].\n\n## New Google Cloud Region for SAP Document AI\n\nSAP Document AI is now available in the Google Cloud region ap30 - Australia (Sydney) [Data: Sources (1687), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 30), (2024, 12, 30))]. This update provides users with access to a new region, enhancing the service's availability and scalability. [Data: Sources (1687), Date_Range ((2024, 12, 30), (2024, 12, 30))].", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2024\n\nThis report provides an overview of SAP BTP's key technologies, highlighting their relationships and significant updates. The information is relevant to SAP BTP's operations as of 2024.\n\n## SAP BTP Technology Landscape\n\nSAP BTP's technology landscape is diverse, with various components and environments supporting different use cases. The company's focus on cloud-based solutions, such as Cloud Foundry and Kyma, enables flexibility and scalability. Effective management of these technologies is crucial for maintaining operational efficiency and innovation. [Data: Sources (1, 2, 3), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Cloud-Based Solutions\n\nSAP BTP's cloud-based solutions, such as Cloud Foundry and Kyma, provide a flexible and scalable platform for developing and deploying applications. These solutions enable companies to respond quickly to changing market conditions and customer needs. [Data: Sources (4, 5, 6), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## SAP Task Center Updates\n\nSAP Task Center has undergone significant updates, including the addition of new task providers and improvements to caching and performance. These updates enhance the user experience and improve operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (7, 8, 9), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Identity and Access Management\n\nSAP BTP's identity and access management solutions, such as Cloud Identity Services, provide secure and efficient access to applications and data. These solutions are critical for maintaining operational security and compliance. [Data: Sources (10, 11, 12), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]\n\n## Document AI Updates\n\nSAP Document AI has undergone significant updates, including the addition of new regions and improvements to performance. These updates enhance the user experience and improve operational efficiency. [Data: Sources (13, 14, 15), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2024, 12, 31))]", "# SAP BTP Technology Overview as of 2025\n\nThis report delves into SAP BTP's key components focusing on technology, illustrating how these entities interact within the organizational framework to uphold regulatory standards and manage financial risks effectively. The information is relevant to the company's operations around 2025.\n\n## Cloud Foundry Environment\n\nThe Cloud Foundry environment at SAP BTP plays a pivotal role in providing a scalable and on-demand platform for deploying applications. Its proactive approach helps safeguard SAP BTP against potential technical pitfalls and ensures continuous compliance with evolving market regulations. Effective management not only prevents technical anomalies but also supports the company's strategic decision-making processes. [Data: Sources (627, 638, 785), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 18))]\n\n## Identity Provisioning\n\nThe Identity Provisioning component at SAP BTP ensures that all user identities are properly managed and secured. Their focus on providing a seamless user experience, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex user access and authentication. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (633, 634, 635), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 18))]\n\n## API Gateway Module\n\nThe API Gateway module at SAP BTP plays a crucial role in managing API access and security. Their focus on providing a robust and scalable API gateway, noted starting 2024, is crucial in maintaining SAP BTP's reputation and operational security, especially in managing complex API access and authentication. Their efforts underscore the commitment to upholding high security standards and ethical practices. [Data: Sources (637, 965, 966), Date_Range ((2024, 01, 01), (2025, 06, 18))]", "# SAP Technology Updates as of 2025\n\nThis report provides an overview of the key updates and changes in SAP technology, focusing on the components and environments that have undergone significant developments. The information is relevant to SAP's technology landscape as of 2025.\n\n## SAP BTP and Cloud Foundry Enhancements\n\nSAP BTP and Cloud Foundry have seen significant updates, including the integration of the SAP Content Agent service with the SAP Cloud Transport Management system. This integration enables the management of theme transport and automation of theme transfer betw